1
00:00:00,584 --> 00:00:02,336
[INARA panting]

2
00:00:02,419 --> 00:00:04,129
This can't be real.

3
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:11,178
[stunned] What is this guy?

4
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:12,471
He's not human!

5
00:00:13,555 --> 00:00:14,473
Damn it!

6
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:16,058
Are you kidding me?

7
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:20,020
[frustrated]

8
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:21,980
[MATSUNAGA]
Kuribayashi! Through!

9
00:00:22,064 --> 00:00:23,190
[gasps]

10
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:26,777
[straining]

11
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,613
[frustrated]

12
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:32,157
[cheering]

13
00:00:32,241 --> 00:00:35,202
[straining] This is nuts!

14
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:37,371
It's like the momentum
we'd built up just up

15
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:39,289
and vanished
in the blink of an eye.

16
00:00:40,624 --> 00:00:42,584
[TOWADA] And it's all
because he joined the game.

17
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:48,382
[amazed]

18
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,177
[ASHITO] When I was a kid,

19
00:00:52,261 --> 00:00:54,638
and I saw
an awesome player on TV-

20
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,516
Even a while back
when I saw Yoshitsune

21
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:59,518
for the first time
on the B team-

22
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:02,271
I was blown away.

23
00:01:02,354 --> 00:01:04,398
I wanted to be like them, but.

24
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:06,775
I feel something-

25
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:09,111
something
that I've never felt before.

26
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:13,240
[ASHITO] I know
no matter how much I want to,

27
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:15,158
I can't be like him.

28
00:01:18,287 --> 00:01:22,082
[♪ upbeat music playing,
10-FEET "Fortress Defense"]

29
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:54,174
I'm trying to follow,
but I can't.

30
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,394
[ASHITO] I don't get
what's happening,

31
00:03:05,477 --> 00:03:06,728
or how it works.

32
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:08,980
None of it.

33
00:03:12,317 --> 00:03:13,568
You're shocked.

34
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:15,696
So are you going to adapt
or give up?

35
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,239
Let's see.

36
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:19,950
[MINAMISAWA] We're not out yet!

37
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:21,451
-[MINAMISAWA] Let's go!
-[gasps]

38
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:22,994
We can still win!

39
00:03:23,078 --> 00:03:24,371
Just focus up

40
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:25,622
and don't quit
thinking on the field!

41
00:03:25,706 --> 00:03:28,125
And remember
what our manager always says.

42
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:30,502
Be a strong person
to be a strong player!

43
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:31,545
[inspired]

44
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:33,213
Right. Yeah!

45
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:34,589
The game's not over!

46
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:36,341
And don't worry
about Kuribayashi.

47
00:03:36,425 --> 00:03:38,093
[MINAMISAWA]
I'll mark him myself.

48
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:40,512
Hey, Yariike!
Go do what you do best!

49
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:42,097
Keep an eye on the back line.

50
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,473
We'll cover the open space.

51
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:47,227
[ASHITO]
What am I thinking?

52
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,688
I'm nowhere near
as good as they are.

53
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:52,107
But I've never been a quitter.

54
00:03:52,524 --> 00:03:54,317
So, how can I help the team out?

55
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:56,278
Come on, brain.

56
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:59,239
Think of something. Anything!

57
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:02,117
[ASHITO] Well, if I don't
understand what's happening,

58
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,161
I need to watch and learn.

59
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:06,329
What do I do in the meantime?

60
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:08,081
I can't just stand here.

61
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,625
Get those thoughts out
of your head, birdbrain!

62
00:04:10,709 --> 00:04:12,169
You're the worst one here!

63
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:14,963
So, there's nothing
you can do to help Kuribayashi!

64
00:04:15,046 --> 00:04:16,715
But if you actually
want to be useful,

65
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,884
then do what I say
until the final whistle,

66
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:19,968
you hear me?

67
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:22,429
[annoyed]

68
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:27,476
[gameplay chatter]

69
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:30,520
[frustrated]

70
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:33,440
[gameplay chatter]

71
00:04:39,321 --> 00:04:40,197
[breathes]

72
00:04:41,198 --> 00:04:42,073
Matsu.

73
00:04:46,578 --> 00:04:48,371
Wait, I understood
what happened!

74
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:51,041
Kuribayashi shook his marker off

75
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:53,043
as soon as his eyes
were on the ball.

76
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:54,377
Damn it!

77
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:56,087
Can we get one goal?

78
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:57,339
Just one?

79
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:59,132
[gameplay chatter]

80
00:04:59,216 --> 00:05:00,509
Oh, I've got you now!

81
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,055
Huh?

82
00:05:05,472 --> 00:05:06,515
[ASHITO] Seriously?

83
00:05:06,598 --> 00:05:07,974
What the heck was that?

84
00:05:08,058 --> 00:05:10,393
It's like the rules of gravity
don't apply to him!

85
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:15,524
[YUMA] Looking for
a one-two, huh?

86
00:05:15,607 --> 00:05:16,650
Way ahead of you!

87
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,068
Oh no, you don't!

88
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,362
[disappointed]

89
00:05:21,488 --> 00:05:22,572
Hang on.

90
00:05:22,656 --> 00:05:24,366
[KANEKO] They're subbing
someone in.

91
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:26,034
They're slowing the game down.

92
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:28,495
-[SUZUMIYA frustrated]
-[SONO] Damn it!

93
00:05:29,621 --> 00:05:31,122
[KURIBAYASHI pondering]

94
00:05:31,206 --> 00:05:34,167
A perfect setup,
but it didn't go as planned.

95
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:37,379
[KURIBAYASHI] On that play,

96
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:39,047
I knew they'd be
cautious of me,

97
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,465
so I made a run
to draw them away

98
00:05:40,549 --> 00:05:41,925
from the goal.

99
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,760
I wanted you
to go forward with the ball

100
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:46,304
and make the shot, Yuma,
not pass it.

101
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:49,182
Well, not much I can do.

102
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:50,559
It's fine.

103
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:52,686
[ASHITO] Kuribayashi.

104
00:05:54,396 --> 00:05:56,565
Um. I saw the play.

105
00:05:56,648 --> 00:05:58,233
Sorry, I could be wrong.

106
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:00,068
But it feels
like you're holding back.

107
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:01,069
[stunned]

108
00:06:02,571 --> 00:06:04,030
[groans]

109
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:06,032
I totally blurted out
what I was thinking.

110
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,285
[ASHITO] Whatever.

111
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:10,287
But to me, it looks
like he's not going all out

112
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:11,413
like I thought he would.

113
00:06:12,247 --> 00:06:13,957
[gentle music]

114
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:16,334
Okay, if I were Kuribayashi,

115
00:06:17,294 --> 00:06:18,628
where would I-

116
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:26,011
Where would I want me to be?

117
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:29,514
[realizing]

118
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:32,392
[whistle blows]

119
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:33,977
All right, he gave us the foul!

120
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,437
let's get a point on the board!

121
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,063
Push up! Push up!

122
00:06:37,147 --> 00:06:38,189
This is our chance!

123
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:39,357
Go for it!

124
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,528
Time's almost up.

125
00:06:43,612 --> 00:06:45,614
This will be
the last kick of the game.

126
00:06:45,697 --> 00:06:47,616
[SUZUMIYA] Come on,
just one goal.

127
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:48,950
We only need one!

128
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:50,493
Let's push up!

129
00:06:51,703 --> 00:06:53,413
[KURIBAYASHI] Spot's wide open.

130
00:06:54,164 --> 00:06:55,498
And so is he.

131
00:06:56,999 --> 00:06:59,628
Number three is standing there
completely unmarked.

132
00:06:59,711 --> 00:07:02,088
But it seems like that doesn't
bother anyone else

133
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:03,506
but me, I guess.

134
00:07:05,175 --> 00:07:06,176
And then.

135
00:07:07,385 --> 00:07:08,678
Nah, let it go.

136
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:10,555
I was planning on scoring
one more time,

137
00:07:11,473 --> 00:07:12,724
but I'd hate to give up a point.

138
00:07:14,392 --> 00:07:15,477
I got number three.

139
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:17,103
[whistle blows]

140
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:18,563
[gameplay chatter]

141
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:20,357
[noticing]

142
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,526
[determined]

143
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,153
[stunned]

144
00:07:28,239 --> 00:07:29,366
I'll be taking that!

145
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:30,408
Kick the ball out-

146
00:07:30,492 --> 00:07:31,368
[ASHITO] To me!

147
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:39,042
[ASHITO] First, point my toes
where I want it to go.

148
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,544
Then aim for the middle
of the ball and-

149
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:43,630
Kick!

150
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:48,551
[KURIBAYASHI] Simply being
in the right place

151
00:07:49,511 --> 00:07:51,262
can kick off a counterattack.

152
00:07:58,103 --> 00:07:59,688
[TAKAGI] Stop him!

153
00:07:59,771 --> 00:08:02,482
Kuribayashi's launching
a solo counterattack!

154
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:04,317
[ALL] Go!

155
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:06,444
[overlapping speeches]

156
00:08:06,528 --> 00:08:08,154
[frustrated]

157
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:09,739
[stunned]

158
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:13,034
[KANEKO] Just one defender.

159
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:15,120
[KAWAJIRI] I've got him.

160
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:16,663
Now stay calm and think.

161
00:08:16,746 --> 00:08:18,998
Worst thing I could do is
jump to get the ball

162
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:20,583
and let him go right past me!

163
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:23,378
[struggling]

164
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:27,090
Good. Way to stay strong.

165
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:29,592
[SUGIURA] Plant yourself there.

166
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,469
Give them time to make it back.

167
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:33,013
[breathes]

168
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:35,056
It'd be nice to have one more.

169
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:39,102
[KURIBAYASHI] One more person
who moves the way I envision.

170
00:08:40,812 --> 00:08:43,148
Oh, well.
Guess that's asking too much.

171
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:44,274
[shocked]

172
00:08:45,734 --> 00:08:48,194
Kuri!

173
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:53,074
[uplifting orchestral music]

174
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,253
[amazed]

175
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:12,010
[cheering]

176
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:14,637
Esperion scores again
off a counterattack!

177
00:09:14,721 --> 00:09:16,097
So awesome!

178
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:19,476
[OHTOMO]
That's the final whistle!

179
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:20,810
We won 3-0!

180
00:09:20,894 --> 00:09:23,271
Kashiwa Dai got spanked
by Esperion!

181
00:09:33,615 --> 00:09:34,657
[MATSUNAGA] Aoi!

182
00:09:34,741 --> 00:09:36,576
I'm impressed, rook!

183
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:39,120
You kicked off a counter
with a killer long ball.

184
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:40,580
Yeah, that was awesome.

185
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:42,499
I heard you practiced
those passes a lot

186
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:43,500
on the B team.

187
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,084
The heavens must be shining down

188
00:09:45,168 --> 00:09:46,211
on you or something.

189
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:49,422
How did you manage
to get into the perfect spot?

190
00:09:49,506 --> 00:09:52,008
[YUMA] Yo, Shimura, you were
really moving out there!

191
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:56,221
What's up?

192
00:09:56,805 --> 00:09:58,515
I thought you would be
a bit happier.

193
00:09:59,057 --> 00:09:59,682
[ASHITO] Oh, uh.

194
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:01,893
When I'm attacking,

195
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:03,770
these images come to me
in an instant,

196
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,396
and that's what happened there.

197
00:10:05,939 --> 00:10:07,732
Yo, dumbass,
mark number ten already!

198
00:10:07,816 --> 00:10:09,192
All right, press him now!

199
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:11,069
[AKUTSU] Box him in! Box him in!

200
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:13,029
But never when I'm defending.

201
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:15,698
[spectating chatter]

202
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:19,118
There you go. Crave it.

203
00:10:19,202 --> 00:10:20,078
[gasps]

204
00:10:20,912 --> 00:10:22,455
I want you to yearn for it.

205
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:26,543
Yearn to defend subconsciously
in the same way you attack.

206
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:27,752
[breathes]

207
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:31,089
That's what I'm talking about.

208
00:10:31,381 --> 00:10:32,298
[annoyed]

209
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:33,216
[unsure]

210
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:36,761
[annoyed]

211
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:45,395
My U-18 Premier League
debut is over.

212
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:47,522
Just like that.

213
00:10:52,402 --> 00:10:54,237
Oh. Hey, we won!

214
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:55,572
Isn't that great?

215
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:58,616
[MIYAKO] By the way,

216
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:00,118
why are you
sneaking around like that?

217
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:01,494
Uh, Hana?

218
00:11:01,578 --> 00:11:02,495
[breathes]

219
00:11:18,136 --> 00:11:22,599
[CROWD cheering and applauding]

220
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:26,144
I'm glad we got
to share the field.

221
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,730
[MINAMISAWA] This guy here
is a first-year.

222
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:30,523
He's never seen you
in action before.

223
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:33,484
I'm so happy it was up close
and personal.

224
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:34,986
Thank you for the match.

225
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:36,571
Now we all can
get even stronger.

226
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:43,161
[KURIBAYASHI] After we scored,
you said

227
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:45,246
"Don't quit thinking
on the field."

228
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:47,081
You didn't give up.

229
00:11:47,165 --> 00:11:49,375
Not until the very
last kick of the game.

230
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:52,545
That was great.

231
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:54,255
[ALL speechless]

232
00:11:56,716 --> 00:11:57,717
[stunned]

233
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:01,471
[TAKASUGI] Everyone.
Thank you for your support.

234
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:03,181
[CROWD applauding]

235
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:06,559
You know,
when Kuribayashi hits the field,

236
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:08,436
most teams
lose their will to fight,

237
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:10,229
or start playing
all reckless-like.

238
00:12:10,313 --> 00:12:12,148
But these guys
were better than that.

239
00:12:12,231 --> 00:12:14,442
They didn't let his presence
change their style.

240
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:15,610
Look at them.

241
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:18,112
[YUMA] They went up
against an elite squad,

242
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:19,322
and never backed down.

243
00:12:19,405 --> 00:12:21,366
I imagine
it must have been refreshing

244
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:23,618
for Kuribayashi to play
against a team like that.

245
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:26,829
Lots of schools will play
these league games

246
00:12:26,913 --> 00:12:28,539
and see it as a chance to train.

247
00:12:28,957 --> 00:12:30,625
That's because most of them
only care

248
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:32,627
about the Inter-High
and National matches.

249
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:35,088
But they played
like their lives

250
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,172
depended on winning.

251
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:38,508
You're right.

252
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:41,386
They left everything
they had on the field.

253
00:12:42,053 --> 00:12:44,555
[emotional music]

254
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:54,649
I've got to do something fast,

255
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,442
or I'm going to be
a waste of space.

256
00:12:57,235 --> 00:12:58,778
There were 11 of us,

257
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:01,072
and ten were playing phenomenal!

258
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:04,158
They all covered for me,
the weak link.

259
00:13:04,242 --> 00:13:05,702
With how I played,

260
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:07,453
I don't have the right

261
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:09,539
to celebrate
today's win with them.

262
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,541
Defending.

263
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:14,335
I've got to get better
at defending,

264
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:16,337
or it's all over for me.

265
00:13:17,505 --> 00:13:19,382
[ASHITO] No,
I won't let it come to that.

266
00:13:20,008 --> 00:13:22,593
If I get the chance
to play in the U-18 again,

267
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:25,346
I'll find a way
to be the best defender

268
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:26,681
they've ever seen.

269
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:28,224
[TAKASUGI] Hey!

270
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:31,686
The manager's calling for you.

271
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:33,604
[ASHITO] Uh, okay.

272
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:36,649
And Aoi.

273
00:13:37,108 --> 00:13:38,776
Huh?

274
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,403
[TAKASUGI] This is just
the beginning for you, okay?

275
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:41,404
Wha?

276
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,574
If you need help,
feel free to ask.

277
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:46,075
[breathes]

278
00:13:47,035 --> 00:13:49,287
You were awesome
out there, Ashito!

279
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:50,705
I am not going to lie,

280
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,373
I was a little worried
at the beginning,

281
00:13:52,457 --> 00:13:54,167
but you didn't give up a goal

282
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,252
and you initiated
an awesome counterattack.

283
00:13:56,336 --> 00:13:59,047
[OHTOMO] Not bad for a debut,
if you ask me!

284
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:01,340
I bet you'll be
on the bench again next time,

285
00:14:01,424 --> 00:14:03,092
You lucky son of a gun!

286
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:05,928
[breathes deeply]

287
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:08,222
[somber music]

288
00:14:08,306 --> 00:14:10,141
[ANRI] Are you honestly
that surprised?

289
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,100
[gasps]

290
00:14:11,434 --> 00:14:12,435
Huh?

291
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:14,437
I suppose so.

292
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,272
You're more small-minded
than I thought.

293
00:14:16,731 --> 00:14:17,774
It's shocking.

294
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:19,317
[TOGASHI] What?

295
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,860
[BOTH stunned]

296
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,653
It's clear from the expression
on your face.

297
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:26,365
You don't quite understand
why Aoi's ahead of you.

298
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:29,368
Just what the hell are you
going on about, princess?

299
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:31,370
And why would I try
to understand something

300
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:32,747
that's not even true?

301
00:14:33,247 --> 00:14:34,290
[breathes]

302
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:38,002
[ANRI] Tell me,
has it ever occurred to you

303
00:14:38,086 --> 00:14:39,796
that you could learn
something from him?

304
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:45,635
[TOGASHI] Where is this
coming from anyway?

305
00:14:46,469 --> 00:14:48,429
What could he show me
that I don't already know?

306
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:51,599
Well, plenty
if you're receptive to learning.

307
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:53,684
But I can tell
from your response just now,

308
00:14:53,768 --> 00:14:56,437
you subconsciously
underestimate Aoi.

309
00:14:57,105 --> 00:15:00,566
[tense music]

310
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:07,532
You know,

311
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:11,452
if you're going to manage
a men's soccer team someday,

312
00:15:11,536 --> 00:15:13,746
you'll have to learn
how to say stuff like that

313
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:16,124
without your
legs shaking all over the place.

314
00:15:16,207 --> 00:15:17,542
[stunned]

315
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:19,752
So how about you
stay out of this woman?

316
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,300
[shocked] Are you
all right, miss?

317
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:27,718
Oh no! Anri, what just happened?

318
00:15:27,802 --> 00:15:28,970
Are you feeling okay?

319
00:15:29,846 --> 00:15:31,764
Say the word
and I'll dispose of him.

320
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:35,726
[shaking]

321
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:41,607
[MIYAKO] Really?

322
00:15:41,691 --> 00:15:43,234
Game's done, so there's
no point in wearing that.

323
00:15:43,985 --> 00:15:44,610
[unsure]

324
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:47,655
And aren't you
Manager Fukuda's little sister?

325
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:49,991
I'm sure they would have
found you better seats

326
00:15:50,074 --> 00:15:51,284
if you had asked them.

327
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,743
[MIYAKO] So why were you sitting

328
00:15:52,827 --> 00:15:54,579
all the way
at the top of the stands?

329
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:55,997
I just was-

330
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,415
don't know much about soccer,

331
00:15:57,498 --> 00:15:59,333
so I didn't want
to distract anyone.

332
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:00,710
But who would you distract?

333
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:03,671
Hold up, is there a player
you're trying to avoid?

334
00:16:05,006 --> 00:16:05,590
[pondering]

335
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:15,474
[flustered]

336
00:16:15,558 --> 00:16:16,476
[anxious]

337
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,437
Hmm?

338
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:22,148
[uneasy]

339
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:23,065
[FUKUDA] Ashito.

340
00:16:26,444 --> 00:16:27,737
[MIYAKO] It's your big brother.

341
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:33,159
[MIYAKO] Hmm?

342
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:35,661
[ASHITO] What's up, old ma-

343
00:16:35,745 --> 00:16:37,288
Manager Fukuda.

344
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:39,040
It's about how I did
today, right?

345
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:40,541
Hear me out.

346
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:43,377
I struggled, it's true.

347
00:16:43,461 --> 00:16:44,962
But I know I'll get there!

348
00:16:45,463 --> 00:16:46,547
So in the next game--

349
00:16:46,631 --> 00:16:48,299
Let me stop you right there.

350
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:50,509
[FUKUDA] If you play like today,
I can't use you.

351
00:16:50,593 --> 00:16:51,177
[shocked]

352
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,261
[BOTH gasps]

353
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,680
[FUKUDA] You won't even
make the bench.

354
00:16:55,932 --> 00:16:58,517
While I do commend you
for stepping up to the task,

355
00:16:58,601 --> 00:17:00,561
your defense
was mediocre at best,

356
00:17:00,645 --> 00:17:02,355
so you must've known
this was coming.

357
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:03,564
Huh?

358
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:05,566
[upset]

359
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:09,320
[ASHITO] We all saw
how much I I sucked.

360
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:11,697
So yeah, I deserve everything
you're saying right now.

361
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,991
Trust me, I know.

362
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:20,206
But to not play in the U-18?
It would be torture!

363
00:17:21,624 --> 00:17:25,127
The intensity of that match.
It burned my skin.

364
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:28,297
Once you've tasted it,
you can't ever go back.

365
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:31,759
Old man.
Please, I'm begging you!

366
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:33,594
One more game, that's it!

367
00:17:34,553 --> 00:17:36,514
I really am onto something here.

368
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:38,099
Just one more chance!

369
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:39,809
I don't even have to play.

370
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:41,310
You can put me on the bench, or-

371
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:42,311
No.

372
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:45,523
It's better if you watch them
from the outside.

373
00:17:45,815 --> 00:17:46,816
[shocked]

374
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:49,443
[BENZEN] We've already got
someone in your spot.

375
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:51,612
Third-year Kobayakawa
was injured,

376
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:53,572
but now
he's totally cleared to go.

377
00:17:53,656 --> 00:17:56,033
He's a defender
who can also play the midfield.

378
00:17:56,117 --> 00:17:58,536
Been our left side fullbacks
since spring,

379
00:17:58,619 --> 00:18:00,288
so he knows how we do things.

380
00:18:00,705 --> 00:18:02,290
So Kuribayashi's back,

381
00:18:02,373 --> 00:18:03,916
and now Kobayakawa,

382
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:05,584
which means
that Esperion will have

383
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:08,045
its strongest
starting lineup for the field.

384
00:18:08,129 --> 00:18:10,673
Both will be training tomorrow,
and I want you to observe.

385
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:12,300
[FUKUDA] I think it'll help.

386
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,051
But good effort out there today.

387
00:18:14,677 --> 00:18:15,970
Now get some rest.

388
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:19,515
[frustrated]

389
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:28,065
[MIYAKO] Are you not
going to say anything to him?

390
00:18:28,733 --> 00:18:30,026
Why should I?

391
00:18:30,401 --> 00:18:31,652
[MIYAKO] Just look at him.

392
00:18:31,736 --> 00:18:33,070
He's bummed out.

393
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:37,199
I remember back
when he played against us.

394
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:39,744
It really appeared
like you understood his game.

395
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:42,163
And today when he came out
on the field.

396
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:43,664
[noticing]

397
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:47,376
Yeah!

398
00:18:48,836 --> 00:18:51,130
[MIYAKO] You were cheering
so loudly for him.

399
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:53,257
Yeah, but why is that
a big deal?

400
00:18:53,341 --> 00:18:54,717
I mean,
I'll cheer for anyone

401
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,510
who plays
on my bro's team, you know?

402
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:57,762
It's called support.

403
00:18:58,471 --> 00:19:00,431
Well, with me being
an athlete myself,

404
00:19:00,765 --> 00:19:02,308
I know how he's feeling now.

405
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:04,477
[MIYAKO] He must
really want to play.

406
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,270
In fact, he's itching for it.

407
00:19:06,354 --> 00:19:07,563
He knows he's close.

408
00:19:08,314 --> 00:19:09,565
But it's the manager's decision.

409
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:11,776
And at times like this,

410
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,694
you come to realize
just how powerless you are.

411
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:17,406
So, you could at least
say something to him.

412
00:19:18,449 --> 00:19:20,034
You've been there before.

413
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:22,578
You know how players feel
because you are one.

414
00:19:24,622 --> 00:19:25,623
Must be nice.

415
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:28,042
[stunned]

416
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,961
But all I can think of
is "good luck."

417
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,380
That's so lame.

418
00:19:33,506 --> 00:19:34,965
I don't know why you feel like

419
00:19:35,049 --> 00:19:36,425
you have to hold back, Hana.

420
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:38,511
Go down there
and speak from the heart.

421
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,721
Just doing that much
will mean a lot to him.

422
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,598
Trust me.

423
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:46,102
[ASHITO]
Your cheering has powers.

424
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,228
Gives me strength.

425
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:49,146
[breathes]

426
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:51,649
What's up?

427
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,484
I saw you out there, Ashito!

428
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:54,860
I know it was rough,

429
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:56,445
but you just keep
working hard, okay?

430
00:19:56,529 --> 00:19:57,446
Hey!

431
00:19:58,239 --> 00:19:59,365
Don't think I forgot!

432
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,491
Why'd you kiss me?

433
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:01,951
[embarrassed]

434
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:02,868
[HANA panicking]

435
00:20:02,952 --> 00:20:04,078
I can't do it!

436
00:20:05,287 --> 00:20:06,414
Uh?

437
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:08,332
Shh.

438
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:10,334
[breathes]

439
00:20:10,418 --> 00:20:11,377
There you are.

440
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,506
You should be
in the locker room

441
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:17,383
changing with the rest
of the team, Aoi.

442
00:20:17,466 --> 00:20:18,467
You okay, Anri?

443
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:20,636
I'm not trying
to be rude, but.

444
00:20:21,804 --> 00:20:23,431
Your face is looking
a little pale.

445
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:24,682
Huh?

446
00:20:25,391 --> 00:20:27,643
Yeah, I just feel
a bit under the weather.

447
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:30,479
[ANRI] That's why
I'm heading home now.

448
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:32,273
Oh, good.

449
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:34,692
[ANRI] You look
pretty tired yourself.

450
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:37,194
Anyway, I brought you this.

451
00:20:37,278 --> 00:20:38,571
[gentle music]

452
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:40,406
I was in the stands
watching you play.

453
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:43,325
And I put together
some notes that should help.

454
00:20:43,409 --> 00:20:45,453
It's mainly tips
about your defending.

455
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:48,664
Remember, defense is
all about shape

456
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:51,500
how you link up with
other players to create them.

457
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,336
Wow. You for real?

458
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,172
Thanks, I really
appreciate this!

459
00:20:56,881 --> 00:20:58,591
[ASHITO] I was having
trouble before

460
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:01,218
and your advice
really helped me out.

461
00:21:01,302 --> 00:21:02,720
You know, about turning my head.

462
00:21:03,471 --> 00:21:05,014
Uh. Yes.

463
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:08,642
You're pretty into this, huh?

464
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,437
I noticed that you're always
coming to see the games.

465
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:12,605
[blushing]

466
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:16,108
And I really owe you
for taking the time

467
00:21:16,192 --> 00:21:17,526
to give me these notes.

468
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:20,488
[happy] Sure.

469
00:21:22,031 --> 00:21:22,656
[noticing]

470
00:21:24,492 --> 00:21:25,367
[gasps]

471
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:27,620
[HANA] You've got a gift.

472
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:29,622
And if you just keep
working hard,

473
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:31,373
then I think you could go pro!

474
00:21:32,333 --> 00:21:33,793
[ANRI] Just keep doing
your best, okay?

475
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:35,294
[breathes]

476
00:21:36,337 --> 00:21:37,254
I will.

477
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:42,760
[BUTLER] Please wait for me!

478
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:44,512
We don't want you to fall again!

479
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:46,222
[running]

480
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:52,436
[gentle melancholy music]

481
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:57,066
[noticing]

482
00:22:02,404 --> 00:22:03,280
[exhales]

483
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:06,158
I miss your face.

484
00:22:06,242 --> 00:22:07,326
Where'd you go?

485
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:12,623
[♪ upbeat music playing,
Ai Higuchi "Triangle"]

486
00:23:39,168 --> 00:23:40,669
[footsteps]

487
00:23:40,753 --> 00:23:43,380
[BENZEN] That Aoi is something.

488
00:23:43,464 --> 00:23:45,549
Not often you get a kid
who's bold enough

489
00:23:45,633 --> 00:23:47,134
to flat-out ask the manager

490
00:23:47,217 --> 00:23:48,677
to put him
on the roster like that.

491
00:23:49,345 --> 00:23:51,305
Man, I love
that kind of enthusiasm.

492
00:23:52,306 --> 00:23:53,641
[BENZEN] Fukuda summoned
a player

493
00:23:53,724 --> 00:23:55,517
to speak to them personally.

494
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:58,187
It's pretty clear he has
high hopes for the boy.

495
00:23:59,730 --> 00:24:01,106
But as of tomorrow,

496
00:24:01,190 --> 00:24:02,566
this Esperion team will have

497
00:24:02,650 --> 00:24:04,401
a real formidable
starting lineup!

498
00:24:04,485 --> 00:24:06,612
Of course, that means
things will be even tougher

499
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,364
for the squad players.

500
00:24:08,447 --> 00:24:10,407
[BENZEN] In other words,
from now on?

501
00:24:10,491 --> 00:24:13,160
There'll be fewer chances
to break into the team.

502
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:17,706
Do you know what the key
component of a strong team is?

503
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:19,708
-I'm disappointed in myself.
-[smirks]

504
00:24:19,792 --> 00:24:21,627
Big talk for guys
not on the team sheet.

505
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,379
[ASARI] Takeshima,
take this one.

506
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:26,048
Ashito. Can you teach
me how you play soccer?

507
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:28,300
I wonder what kind of
defending they'll show me.

